WEBVTT

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.650
Good morning, everyone!

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.270
Hey.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.650
Morning.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.030
Morning, Nadeshiko-chan.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.200
Akari-chan, it's been ages!

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.410
It sure has.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.790
Let's have fun today, Nadeshiko-chan.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.760
Yeah, we will!

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.790
Let's relax and heal at 
the capybara hot spring!

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.290
Yeah!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.820
Thank you for looking 
after my sister, Sensei.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.800
Of course. I'll take good care of her.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.050
Shall we get going, then?

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.780
Yeah!

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.430
See you, Onee-chan!

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.670
Don't go causing Sensei any trouble.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.690
Listen up, kids.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:01:00.290
Our main theme of this trip is to visit 
some geoparks and try Izu's local food.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.910
Rin and I are going to 
check out <i>all</i> the geosites.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.170
She's already on her way.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.580
We can't let her leave us in the dust.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.290
Yessir!

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>Geoparks are natural parks 
rich in geographic assets,</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:19.970
<i>such as volcanoes, geological 
features, and landscapes.</i>

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:26.230
<i>Each of those assets is known 
as a "geosite" or "geospot."</i>

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.340
It's been forever since we 
went camping together!

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.230
It's been since the Christmas trip, hasn't it?

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:37.780
Also, Nadeshiko, is it just me, or do 
you have huge bags under your eyes?

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.660
I was so giddy last night, I couldn't sleep.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.240
Are you all right?

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.660
I'm fine!

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.500
There's no way I could sleep 
when we're going Izu camping!

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.080
You're not getting any sleep 
tonight either, Akari-chan!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.630
Yeah, figures.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:37.940
<b>(2) Episode 10
The Izu Camp Trip Begins!</b>

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.760
<i>I really like the sea.</i>

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:50.500
Cape Ose

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.490
<i>Geospot number one: Cape Ose.</i>

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:50.500
<i>A narrow strip of land formed from 
dirt and rubble carried by currents.</i>

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.030
Floresta 
Yakushin

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:07.030
Kamike Pond

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.780
There it is.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:41.070
Jouyama

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.090
Geospot number two: Jouyama.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:40.550
<i>One of Izu's most famous mountains, formed 
by upthrusts of magma from tectonic activity.</i>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.630
It looks like a fist from the side.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:46.930
You're right.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:51.240
Hey, look, Nadeshiko-chan! 
It's a huge knuckle mountain!

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.390
She won't wake up...

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.050
I'm sure she will by the 
time we get to Shimoda.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:09.720
Good morning!!

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.610
We're in Izu now.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.320
NO SLEEP!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.350
Her eyes are wide awake.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.260
<i>Must be easy in the van.</i>

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.960
<i>Fifty more kilometers to Shimoda...</i>

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.600
Okay.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.730
<i>What a crazy mountain pass.</i>

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.430
<b>Mind
manners
and
rules</b>

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.550
<i>It's a huge shrimp in the mountains.</i>

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.040
Shrimp...

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.650
<b>Roadside station</b>

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:06.150
<b>Wasabi Mountain</b>

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:06.150
<b>Have some
wasabi!</b>

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:26.280
Kawazu Nanadaru Loop Bridge

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.880
<i>Geospot number three: Ryugukutsu Cave.</i>

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:49.300
Ryugukutsu Cave

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:49.300
<i>Waves have eroded the roof of 
this cave, creating a skylight.</i>

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.520
Wow...

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.320
We aren't moving at all.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:09.950
The cherry blossom festival in Kawazu City 
is notorious for causing traffic jams.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:14.780
<i>A cherry blossom festival 
is held in Kawazu City</i>

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.370
<i>from the beginning of February 
to the beginning of March.</i>

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.120
<i>Each year, a million 
people come from all over</i>

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.560
<i>to enjoy the earliest-blooming
 cherry blossoms in Japan.</i>

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.960
I'm back!

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:34.240
Stuck in traffic

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:28.590
That was fun.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.130
I got some cherry blossom 
steamed buns for us.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.520
I thought you were going to the restroom.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.830
I should tell Rin we're going to be late.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.850
I'm at Shimoda.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.540
Where are you guys?

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:45.730
We're stuck in traffic because of 
the Kawazu Cherry Blossom Festival.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.730
We're going to be a bit late.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.900
Sorry.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.150
Okay.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.740
I'll wander around to kill time.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.990
<i>That's a huge anchor.</i>

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.870
<b>Shimoda Hot Springs
Kaiyu Foot Bath</b>

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:05.750
<i>So warm.</i>

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:13.320
<i>I like toriis by the water.</i>

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.080
<i>It's the Black Ships!</i>

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.140
<i>The Black Ships are here!</i>

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.150
<i>Maybe I'll go check it out over there.</i>

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.140
Nadeshiko-chan! Nadeshiko-chan!

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.890
Nadeshiko-chan!

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:33.710
You're finally awake!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.490
Sorry... I fell asleep.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:37.910
Where are we?

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.160
We're all done camping.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.160
We're about to head back to Yamanashi.

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:42.810
What?

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:46.640
You were asleep for two whole days.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:47.750
Two days?!

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:51.000
I kept trying to wake you up.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:53.130
You gotta keep up.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:57.140
I bought you some souvenirs, 
and we got tons of pictures.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.720
Let's look at them on our way home.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:08:59.710
Yeah.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.700
I-Izu camping...

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.400
Stop tormenting Nadeshiko, you lying sisters.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.150
Rin!

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.530
Sorry we're late, Shima-san.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.580
Not at all.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.910
Thank you for driving, Sensei.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.290
Riding so far must've been tough.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.040
What route did you take?

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.920
I drove down West Izu, by the water.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:35.010
Rin-chan...

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.430
Where am I?

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.040
What day is it?

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.930
A-Are you all right, Nadeshiko?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.350
Time to eat!

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.520
Yum!

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:56.990
The sweet-and-spicy sauce and the camembert 
cheese work so well with the fried alfonsino.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:57.860
Right?

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:01.200
I've always wanted to try this.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.580
I can die happy now.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.580
There must be more you want to do first.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:10.070
Hey, it looks like octopus legs.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.130
It's a crayfish.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.380
That's a shrimp.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.380
You even went to Ryugukutsu Cave, huh?

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:20.510
Jouyama was about the only geospot 
we got to see along the way.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.220
We bought some raw wasabi at 
the roadside station, though.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.080
Yeah! The wasabi ice cream was great!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.890
Wasabi ice cream?!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.400
I want some, too!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.940
Izu's known for wasabi ice cream.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.530
There'll be plenty more on the way.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.950
Oh, the loop bridge was fun, too.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.910
It was like a roller coaster.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.160
Whoa.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:48.830
The real "whoa" here is that all 
the rocking didn't wake you up.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:01.980
Rin visited two geospots, 
and we visited one.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.600
We can't make it to all of them, 
but it'd be nice to see the big ones.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.930
Yeah.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:10.020
Are we going to the Dougashima 
tombolo the day after tomorrow?

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:10.890
Yeah.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.810
I heard it's best right around noon.

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:15.480
Aoi-chan, what's a tombolo?

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:17.570
It's a kind of pork jowl.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.950
What's it taste like?

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.660
Lying comes as easily to Inuko as breathing.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:27.200
And Mini Inuko lies about not 
knowing what a tombolo is.

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:30.160
This is how the lying sisters work.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.210
So scary, Aki-chan...

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.960
You two are overthinking it.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.260
All right, let's go shopping 
for camp supplies.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.720
Woo!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.220
Woo.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.220
<b>Open 24 hours</b>

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:01.610
<b>Manpuku Shoten</b>

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.610
Is that it, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.490
Yup. Premium Shimoda...

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.000
dried alfonsino!

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:12.300
It's been a while, but we're going 
to use this to make some camp grub!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.500
I can't wait for dinner.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.530
<b>Booze Ban
Day 25</b>

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.060
No drinking yet.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.610
You know what to do, Rin.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.900
Operation Shrimp.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.650
Y-Yeah.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.910
Rin, Ena, hear me out.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.900
Nadeshiko and Inuko are on dinner 
duty for the first night of camping.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:53.320
They're going to be making <i>something </i>
using local Izu dried alfonsino.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.140
The second night, dinner is on us three.

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:59.940
Thus, their birthday celebration 
will occur on night two.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.420
Regarding the menu...

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:06.800
I'm made aware that Shimoda 
is known for its spiny lobster.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:10.230
Spiny lobsters, along with alfonsino,
 bring good fortune.

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:14.310
I want to make a nice 
spiny lobster dinner for them.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:17.770
But alfonsino and spiny lobster 
are both fine dining.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:20.980
Buying both will surely blow our budget.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:23.780
Thus, I have come up with a plan:

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:28.200
We'll make Sensei give up drinking and use 
her booze money to buy spiny lobster.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.200
<i>What a slimy plan.</i>

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.540
This will be known as "Operation Shrimp."

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:33.940
Don't forget.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:42.340
<i>Now, how do we talk her into it?</i>

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:46.300
Excuse me. I'd like this dried spiny lobster.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.590
<i>She's already buying it!</i>

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.230
Saitou-san told me about cooking 
something with spiny lobster.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:58.250
Laid the groundwork already

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:00.020
Not bad, Ena.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:03.230
We should have just asked 
normally from the beginning.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.950
We're almost at Cape Tsumeki.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.870
This is one of the geospots, huh?

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:12.830
Yes.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:16.370
I've been winter camping here with 
my family a few times in the past.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:20.420
There's no campsite here, though.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:22.380
We're camping out by the beach.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:26.840
There's a bylaw prohibiting 
camping between June and October

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:29.630
<b>No Camping</b>

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.640
along all the beaches in Izu.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:34.510
But between November and May,
the ban is lifted.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.270
I never knew.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.600
No wonder you teach social studies.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:39.940
Yeah.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.020
There's no camping allowed here.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:43.830
What?

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:46.260
Um...

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:53.530
<b>Shimoda Ward
Information Center</b>

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:49.360
I checked with the city,

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.490
and they told me that it's 
permitted during the winter.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.530
About that...

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:58.790
The land owner instituted a ban on winter 
camping as well, as of a few years ago.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:02.000
Wh-What do we do?

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:08.820
Cape Tsumeki

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:06.800
<i>Geospot number four: Cape Tsumeki.</i>

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:10.880
<i>A cape southeast of Shimoda City,
 on Suzaki Peninsula.</i>

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:14.800
<i>The area is known for its narcissus colonies.</i>

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.070
I really love the sea.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.400
Yeah.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:30.780
Watching the sea really cleanses your mind—

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:38.850
Tawaraiso
Beach

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:41.830
These rocks are so blocky. Weird.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.830
One of nature's mysteries.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:49.600
<b>Dainagon
Chunky Red Bean Soup</b>

00:15:56.450 --> 00:16:01.020
I'm sorry. I'm looking for 
a campsite for us right now.

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.400
You don't need to get so down, Sensei.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:10.610
<i>I was hoping to get my 
drink on all day today...</i>

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:14.280
Maybe there are some open 
spots at the campsites today.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.490
It's winter, after all.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:21.460
We have to find one quick, though, 
or the administrators will all go home.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.830
That's what happened at Lake Yamanaka, right?

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:29.000
We could end up having to sleep in the car!

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.010
Sleeping in the car...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.300
I'm sleeping up there?

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:41.270
Hey, why don't we try asking Iida-san?

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:44.850
She's a veteran camper, and she's a local.

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.020
That's it!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.400
Hello, Iida Liquors.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.280
Oh, from Lake Yamanaka!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:55.830
What's happening?

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:04.620
Iida-san has an acquaintance 
who runs a campsite.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.670
They found us a place there.

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.250
Yay!

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.340
Where's the campsite?

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:12.920
By the beach in Nishiizu City.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:17.300
That's pretty close to Dougashima, 
where we were gonna go the day after next.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:20.970
In that case, let's chill until 
noon and go tomorrow.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:24.480
We're going to have to make a huge detour

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.810
to get to the geospot tomorrow, though.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:28.060
You're right.

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:30.070
May I?

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:34.610
We could visit this geospot right now,
 before we go to the campsite.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.570
Then, tomorrow, 
we could make our way up slowly

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:40.080
and stop by Itou on our 
way home the day after.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.830
That's a perfect route!

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.580
Wow, Rin-chan!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:47.330
You sure are an expert traveler, Shima-san.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:49.540
Well, shall we get going?

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:50.840
Yeah!

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:57.080
This way, we'll have plenty 
of time tomorrow to prep.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.590
For Operation Shrimp.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:17:59.800
I see.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.350
Good thinking, Rin.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:02.850
What's up?

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.280
We should let Mini Inuko in on it, too.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:21.140
<b>Ultra Fresh
Juice</b>

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:21.140
<b>Izu Orange Center</b>

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:27.890
Mandarin
Wine

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:47.890
Over there!

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:51.360
Wow!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.340
This place is amazing!

00:18:53.790 --> 00:19:04.810
Hosono Plateau

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:57.320
<i>Geospot number five: Hosono Plateau.</i>

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:04.540
<i>A highland in Inatori, Higashiizu City, 
well-known for its fields of silver grass.</i>

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:07.370
We kind of missed the season, huh?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.540
Same for the narcissus of Cape Tsumeki.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.540
It's a small price to pay.

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:26.760
<i>It's so pretty...</i>

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:31.290
<i>I'm glad I came this far by bike.</i>

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:42.450
We're finally here.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.950
15-minute walk from here to 
the peak of Mt. Misujiyama 
Give it a shot! 
*Great views along the way

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:45.660
This says it's fifteen minutes to the peak.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:47.860
It's a mini mountain climb.

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:48.650
Indeed.

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:50.500
Nadeshiko-chan!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.120
Let's race to the top!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.710
Okay! Challenge accepted!

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:57.630
The loser has to buy the winner a drink.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:58.630
All right!

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.470
Hold it, hold it, hold it...

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:04.220
Count me in, too!

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.180
So full of life.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:08.600
They sure are.

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:11.940
Okay, we'll see you up ahead.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.190
Okay.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:15.230
We'll be taking our time.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:17.360
Are you sure, Aki?

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.670
This is Nadeshiko-chan you're up against.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:22.470
I got this.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:28.490
<i>I'm not the same girl who got 
winded on the hill at Fuefuki.</i>

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:33.440
<i>My legs are super strong now, after 
all that work at the end of the year.</i>

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.130
Okay, this'll be the starting line.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.670
Ready...

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:41.650
<i>Now is the moment you get to witness...</i>

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:42.950
Go!

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.840
<i>...the evolved Aki!</i>

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.640
What a nice view.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:02.770
Yeah.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:06.030
Mountain climbing is nice for a change.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.270
Yeah.

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:11.070
Are you not interested in mountain 
climbing at all, Rin-chan?

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:12.900
Mountain climbing, huh?

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:17.980
I don't think I could be one of those legit 
climbers who carries a ton of stuff with them.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:22.450
But I think I'd like to stay at a 
campsite for climbers someday.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:29.860
Once it gets warmer, I guess.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:33.250
It really is a nice view.

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:36.170
I want to come back again when 
the silver grass is in season.

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:37.650
Same.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:46.410
Well, should we get going?

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:47.910
I guess we should.

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:54.290
Aki-chan's dead.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:34.450
Next Episode

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:34.450
<b>Izu Camping!! On the Way</b>

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:41.260
When camping...

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:41.260
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:41.260
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:41.260
Outdoor Activities Club
